/// NOTE: Most readers (including authors of hardware drivers that allocate or
/// use buffers) are likely looking for [`fuchsia.sysmem2/Allocator`], NOT this
/// library.
///
/// This library (`fuchsia.hardware.sysmem`) defines privileged backend
/// registration protocols used ONLY by:
///   1. Drivers that implement and register a custom external sysmem heap
///      (via [`fuchsia.hardware.sysmem/Sysmem.RegisterHeap`]).
///   2. The platform secure memory (TEE) driver that registers physical secure
///      heaps (via [`fuchsia.hardware.sysmem/Sysmem.RegisterSecureMem`]).
///
/// Security model:
/// [`fuchsia.hardware.sysmem/Sysmem`] is a high-privilege protocol. Sysmem
/// trusts any client connected to this protocol. Access is restricted via
/// Component Framework capability routing: ONLY components that specifically
/// and legitimately need to call `RegisterHeap` or `RegisterSecureMem` should
/// be routed / permitted to `use` `fuchsia.hardware.sysmem.Sysmem`.
@available(added=HEAD)
library fuchsia.hardware.sysmem;
